<section class="sec" id="monorepos" aria-labelledby="t-mono">
  <h2 id="t-mono"><span class="n">6</span> Whole repositories, monorepos included</h2>
  <p class="lede"><span class="nt"><code>audit</code> finds every package</span> by its manifest, from <code>package.json</code> to <code>go.mod</code>, <code>Cargo.toml</code> or <code>pyproject.toml</code>, and shows which ones nothing documents. The agent writes the root pages with a map of the packages first, then one package at a time, so even a large monorepo fits.</p>
  <aside class="mn"><b>Not your dependencies</b>The root is the repository, not a package, and copied dependencies such as <code>node_modules</code> or <code>vendor</code> are skipped.
    <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/paquetes.py#detectar -->
  </aside>
  <div class="wide">
<figure class="termwin">
<figcaption class="termbar"><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>zsh — dockeeper audit</figcaption>
